# Example witness for circuit/reanchoring_witness/src/main.nr, at count=4
# (padded to N_MAX=256 -- see main.nr's doc for why the arrays are 256-long
# even though only the first `count` entries are real).
#
# Same underlying fixture as circuit/reanchoring/Prover.toml.example --
# running `nargo execute witness` here prints the exact Header lines (with
# prev_hash filled in) for the first `count` real headers, since both crates
# share the same hash_header (real Poseidon2 sponge). This crate's job is
# only to derive prev_hash from raw per-header data (types.RecoveryHeader,
# no prev_hash stored) -- it never itself produces a proof, and never itself
# pads (that's scripts/reanchoring_prover/prove_and_submit.sh's job when
# building the real circuit's Prover.toml).
#
# To use: cp Prover.toml.example Prover.toml, then `nargo execute witness`,
# and grep the printed `Header { ... }` lines into the real circuit's
# Prover.toml (scripts/reanchoring_prover/prove_and_submit.sh does this
# automatically against real chain data).

